provider_responses.text:
Send this message now:

> Hi, my check-in date would be [DATE] and my email is [EMAIL].  
> Before I send my ID or make any payment, please send me:
> 1. the full property address and room details;  
> 2. a draft rental contract with the landlord/agency name, rent, deposit, and dates;  
> 3. your company NIF/registration details, if you are an agency;  
> 4. confirmation of who will receive the deposit and why that account holder is authorized to receive it;  
> 5. a time for a live video viewing of the room.  
> Once these are confirmed, I can proceed quickly.

Then use this checklist.

### Green flags
Proceed cautiously if they:
- give the exact address;
- send a coherent contract draft;
- provide a company name/NIF that you can independently check;
- agree to a live video viewing;
- accept payment only after signing;
- have the deposit paid to the landlord/agency named in the contract;
- answer direct questions clearly without rushing you.

### Stop signs
Do **not** send money or ID if they:
- refuse to give the address;
- say you must pay before viewing or receiving a contract;
- push urgency: “many people want it,” “pay in the next hour,” etc.;
- ask for crypto, gift cards, cash transfer, or payment to an unrelated name;
- send a contract with missing address, missing landlord identity, or unclear deposit-refund terms;
- will not do a live video call;
- demand an unwatermarked ID immediately.

### If you decide to send ID
Use a watermarked copy. Write across it:

> **For rental application only — [agency/property name] — [today’s date] — not for other use**

Send only the ID page/card they actually require. Do not send:
- bank statements;
- card details;
- passwords or verification codes;
- a selfie holding your ID unless you have independently verified the agency and know why it is needed.

### Before paying the deposit
Confirm these exact facts in writing:

- Property address: `[address]`
- Room: `[room description]`
- Start/check-in date: `[date]`
- Monthly rent: `€[amount]`
- Deposit: `€[amount]`
- Deposit refund conditions: `[terms]`
- Recipient name and IBAN: `[name / IBAN]`
- Contract landlord/agency name: `[name]`

If the recipient name does not match the contract, pause. Ask:

> “The contract names [X], but the payment account is in the name of [Y]. Please provide written confirmation and documentation showing that [Y] is authorized to receive the deposit for this tenancy.”

No clear documentation = no payment.

